    "headline": "Royal Enfield teases the Himalayan 750 ahead of an EICMA reveal in Milan",
    "text": "Royal Enfield has released the first official teaser for the Himalayan 750: an adventure motorcycle and rider silhouetted against a red sky. There is no name or spec sheet, only map coordinates for central Milan, which points to a reveal at EICMA, held from November 3 to 8. The bike is expected to use a new 750cc twin-cylinder engine with touring-focused equipment, making it Royal Enfield's largest-capacity motorcycle yet. It is expected to rival the Norton Atlas and the Triumph Tiger Sport 660.",
    "why": "Royal Enfield's bigger bikes have been losing sales even as the brand grows. A 750cc adventure tourer is its answer at the top.",
